{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> The emissary of Yitro to Moses." "<b>I am your father-in-law Yitro</b> etc. And if you ask: Yitro, who was very humble, as we find that he said to Moses, 'Why do you sit alone?' — is it conceivable that he would send things like this to one as great as Moses? Rather, the clouds of glory surrounded Israel, and the emissaries would enter inside the cloud, and he would tie the letter to an arrow and shoot it inside. Tanḥuma."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:27.363425157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}